{"id": "192683", "revid": "79572", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=192683", "title": "Geidam", "text": "Geidam is a town in Yobe State, North East Nigeria.\nUnderstand.\nGeidam is a town with an approximate area of 4,357 km\u00b2 and a population of 157,295 according to the 2006 census.\nGet in.\nGeidam is connected to other towns and cities by road, though transport options can be limited due to the rural nature of the region. Minibuses and shared taxis are common means of reaching Geidam from nearby cities like Damaturu (the state capital), Maiduguri in Borno State, and Gashua."}
