{"id": "194371", "revid": "2350368", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=194371", "title": "Upper Assam", "text": "Upper Assam (\u0989\u099c\u09a8\u09bf \u0985\u09b8\u09ae \"Ujoni Osom\") is a region in Assam, India. This consists of Biswanath, Golaghat, Lakihmpur, Majuli, Jorhat, Sivasagar, Dhemaji, Dibrugarh, Charaideo and Tinsukia districts.\nUnderstand.\nUpper Assam forms the easternmost reach of the Brahmaputra Valley, bordered by Arunachal Pradesh and Nagaland. Historically the political and cultural core of the Ahom Kingdom\u2014which ruled the region for roughly six centuries\u2014it is defined today by vast tea estates, petroleum heritage, riverine wetlands, and dense semi-evergreen rainforests. Major urban hubs include Jorhat, Dibrugarh, and Tinsukia.\nGet in.\nBy train.\nUpper Assam is well served by the Northeast Frontier Railway:\nEat.\nAssamese cuisine focuses on delicate, aromatic, and sour flavors rather than heavy spices:"}
{"id": "194383", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=194383", "title": "G\u00f6\u00dfweinstein", "text": "G\u00f6\u00dfweinstein is a village in Upper Franconia.\nUnderstand.\nBuilt above the River Wiessent.\nGet in.\nBy car.\nG\u00f6\u00dfweinstein is 2 km from the B470 between Pegnitz and Forchheim. Accessible via the A73 motorway between Bamberg and Nuremberg.\nGo next.\nFollow the P\u00fcttlach River gorge 9.5 km along the B470 west to Pottenstein or east 29 km to Forchheim"}
